# A female's appetite lights
# The four lights on a female that show how hungry she is: her head, which follows
# whichever appetite is the stronger; her orange belly (her O appetite); her greenish
# belly (her P appetite); and her feet, which show which of the two is currently winning.
# Watch one female from switch-on and you should see exactly this.

0 Her head, her two belly lights and her feet are switched on, but head and belly are at zero brightness. Only her feet show immediately.
-> one-appetite-rising : O appetite, orange belly
-> one-appetite-rising : P appetite, greenish belly
2.4 Two and a half seconds later head and belly show their first real value: head lit in proportion to her stronger appetite, each belly light in proportion to its own. As with the males this is very dim at first.
0 Her feet take a colour rather than a brightness, at fixed brightness: orange while her P appetite is ahead, greenish while her O appetite is ahead or the two are equal. Her feet are the one light on her you can read across the room from the first second.
0 Female 1 starts with P far ahead, so her feet are orange. Female 3 starts with O ahead, so hers are greenish. Female 2 starts with both equal, so hers are greenish too and may flicker as one appetite briefly gets ahead of the other.
224 Head and belly brighten one small step every 2.4 seconds, continuously, until all three are full.
0 Because both appetites climb at the same speed, the one that started behind never catches up - until they both hit the ceiling of 100 and become equal. Female 1's feet therefore turn from orange to greenish just under four minutes after switch-on, and from then on all three females have greenish feet for the rest of the evening. An easy thing to check: no female should still have orange feet ten minutes in.
